  "solution": {
    "text": "Physisorption is exothermic in nature. Therefore, in accordance with Le-Chatliers principle, it decreases with increase in temperature. This means physisorption occurs at low temperature more readily. So, The correct order of temperature for curves I, II, III, IV are :<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>T</mtext> <mn>4</mn> </msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub> <mtext>T</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub> <mtext>T</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub> <mtext>T</mtext> <mn>1</mn>&nbsp;</msub></mrow></math>"
